:null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested on Godot Version 4.4.1 and 4.5 Beta 3.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta3.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7602) - AMD Ryzen 7 9800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.62 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nResources with the [Tool] flag incorrectly interpret C# Enum : byte as Signed Byte in inconsistent ways.\n\nEx: In menu displays, selecting a value above 128 correctly shows the enum name.  However selecting the value, instead displays the negative signed numeric value in the resource display, and the resulting .tscn will save a negative, signed value to the resource.\n\nThis seems to mostly(?) be a visual bug, as accessing the values via C# seems to return the correct enum value.  However, I don't know/can't test all possible situations where this might create issues.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee Minimum reproduction project attached.\n\n>Select the Non-Tool Resource.\n>Select values above 127 for the fields/properties of the resource.\n>Observe the correct enum value display.\n\n>Select the Tool Resource.\n>Select values above 127 for the fields/properties of the resource.\n>Observe the incorrect, signed negative byte value displayed, rather than the Enum value.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[ByteEnumResourceBugProject.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21171869/ByteEnumResourceBugProject.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","f